<title>NETHERLANDS: SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates down at end-Oct.</title>
<headline>SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates down at end-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>SGS Warehouse Services gave the following estimates of cocoa beans in store in Europe as of the end of October/early November. All figures in tonnes.</p>
<p>			Total	  Of which for the buffer stock</p>
<p>Amsterdam	   410,000	     42,953.787</p>
<p>Hamburg/Bremen     97,500	     15,512.218</p>
<p>UK (all ports)     41,750		4,083.467</p>
<p>Antwerp		75,500		2,433.933</p>
<p>Rotterdam	    12,850		9,740.066</p>
<p>The data gives the following changes on month-ago levels:</p>
<p>Amsterdam	 down  21,500</p>
<p>Hamburg/Bremen  down   5,250</p>
<p>UK (all ports)  down   2,250</p>
<p>Antwerp	   down   1,500</p>
<p>Rotterdam	 down     650</p>
<p>-Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
